## Pictures (D471, 2026-10-24: real EA art for every weapon)

**The owner's decision (2026-10-24, D471):** use real official EA / Battlefield 6
art for every weapon, take the best real image found, and record its source; the
licence is his to settle later. So, for Battlefield 6 only, a picture may come
from the Battlefield wiki (battlefield.fandom.com, files served from
static.wikia.nocookie.net) **when the file is EA's own art**: the wiki tags
these files `{{EA}}` / `{{Fairuse}}`. **All of them are EA-owned art: flag for
the owner.** The order taken, best first:

1. **EA's Battlefield Portal weapon icons** ("BF6 <gun> Portal Icon.png",
   512 x 256, transparent side views, the same look as the other games' pictures);
2. **EA's gadget renders** ("Battlefield 6 <gadget>.png", transparent);
3. **the in-game armory renders** of the default finish ("<gun> Factory BF6.png",
   "<melee> Standard Issue BF6.png"), on the armory's curtain;
4. **EA's own site pictures** (drop-assets.ea.com, the 2026-10-21 pass), where
   nothing above exists (Season 2 to 5 guns that Portal does not show yet).

Each is trimmed to the weapon, fitted inside 480 x 300 and saved as a 128-colour
PNG (78 pictures, about 1.9 MB; the 31 before were 5.5 MB). The 2026-10-21
crops of EA's promotional screenshots (M4A1, M87A1 in a soldier's hands) were
replaced by Portal icons. **No picture (image: null):** Mk 24, RSPR, Z84M, M136 AT, Ripper 14", Hunting Knife. Mk 24, RSPR and
Z84M (Season 5, 2026-10-13) have no EA picture anywhere yet; the M136 AT's
render is referenced on the wiki but never uploaded; the Ripper 14" and the
Hunting Knife have none.

**M320A1 HE** shows EA's M320A1 THRM render: it is the same launcher (HE, THRM
and SMK are its rounds). **Combat Knife** shows the KBR Mark II, the default
knife (the catalog's uncertain note).

